| 6.25% | {{ phase13.analysis.conditions.quest_6_25.easy.retention | pct }} [{{ phase13.analysis.conditions.quest_6_25.easy.retention_ci95.0 | pct }}–{{ phase13.analysis.conditions.quest_6_25.easy.retention_ci95.1 | pct }}] | {{ phase13.analysis.conditions.quest_6_25.hard.retention | pct }} [{{ phase13.analysis.conditions.quest_6_25.hard.retention_ci95.0 | pct }}–{{ phase13.analysis.conditions.quest_6_25.hard.retention_ci95.1 | pct }}] | **{{ phase13.analysis.conditions.quest_6_25.verdict | str }}** | {{ phase13.analysis.conditions.quest_6_25.gap_ci95.0 | pp }} to {{ phase13.analysis.conditions.quest_6_25.gap_ci95.1 | pp }} |

**At 6.25% the shortfall is established.** With five times the prompts, the two intervals no longer
overlap, which Phase 12's 30 prompts at this context could not show.

**At 12.5% it is not, by the pre-committed rule.** The two intervals still overlap. The difference CI
excludes zero, but that test was introduced after Phase 12's data was read, and this phase does not
promote it to the rule after the fact. The honest statement is that a shortfall at 12.5% is likely
and not established.

**The effect is smaller than Phase 12 estimated.** At 30 prompts, Phase 12 put the 32K gap at
{{ phase13.analysis.conditions.quest_12_5.phase12_gap_at_30 | pp }} (12.5%) and
{{ phase13.analysis.conditions.quest_6_25.phase12_gap_at_30 | pp }} (6.25%); at
{{ phase13.analysis.summary.prompts_per_kind.vt | int }} prompts it is
{{ phase13.analysis.conditions.quest_12_5.gap | pp }} and
{{ phase13.analysis.conditions.quest_6_25.gap | pp }}. Small samples overstate effects that clear a
bar, and this is that shrinkage. [Phase 12](PHASE_12.md)'s 32K numbers should be read through this
table.

Scored all-or-nothing (Phase 12's post-hoc view), Quest-style selection completes the whole chain on
{{ phase13.analysis.conditions.quest_12_5.hard.retention_all_or_nothing_post_hoc | pct }} (12.5%) and
{{ phase13.analysis.conditions.quest_6_25.hard.retention_all_or_nothing_post_hoc | pct }} (6.25%) of
the prompts the full cache solves.

